{{Culture of Balisca}}

The '''[[W:National coat of arms|coat of arms]] of Balisca''' ({{Lang-bl|Escudo de armas de Balisca}}) is the heraldic emblem and one of the official symbols of the [[Baliscan Confederation]]. It was adopted on 17 October 1919, following the [[1919 Confederal Convention]]. 

The arms consist of a white star, with a superimposed [[W:Chaco eagle|crowned solitary eagle]] with outstretched wings. The eagle holds a [[W:Sickle|sickle]] in its right claw and a [[W:Hammer|hammer]] ("[[W:Hammer and sickle|hammer and sickle]]") in its left, crossed. On the chest of the eagle is a shield with a sunset behind three green mountains, with three [[W:Architectural terracotta|terracotta]] towers. The towers and hills symbolize the three founding republics ([[Cerdanya]], [[Hesperia]] and [[Bayara]]), while the sunset represents the evening star ([[W:Hesperus|Hesperus/Vesper]]).

Bundles of [[Balisca#Etymology|açaí berries]] on the right side of the star, and stalks of [[W:Flint corn|flint corn]] on the left side are connected at the bottom by a ribbon with floating tips, in red, which contains the official motto of the confederation - ''Solidaridad y Libertad'' ({{Lang-bl|Solidarity and Freedom}}).

